## 🤖 Agent Harness Layer (dual harness — CORRECTION 42)

> Kept deliberately short: this rule loads in every Cursor and Claude Code session.
> The reasoning lives in the ADRs, not here.

- **One contract.** `AGENTS.md` is the behaviour source. `CLAUDE.md` = `@AGENTS.md` +
  Claude-only addenda. Keep Claude Code's `/config` → *Project instructions* on the
  default (`claude-md-or-agents-md`): the load-both mode is expected to double-load
  `AGENTS.md` alongside the import — confirm with `/memory` before ever changing it.
- **Generated ≠ edited.** `.claude/agents/`, `.claude/output-styles/` and `.claude/rules/`
  are build outputs — edit the source (`.github/docs/prompts/agents/`, `.cursor/rules/`),
  then `make claude-gen`. Drift is blocked by pre-commit and re-checked in CI.
- **Enforcement lives in config.** `.claude/settings.json` permissions + `hooks/guard.py`.
  Prose in `CLAUDE.md` or a rule is guidance, not a boundary (CORRECTION 39 §11).
- **Commit:** `settings.json`, `hooks/`, `skills/`, `agents/`, `rules/`, `output-styles/`.
  **Never commit:** `**/.claude/settings.local.json`, `**/CLAUDE.local.md`,
  `**/.claude/agent-memory-local/` (see the `.gitignore` block below).
- **Privacy boundary.** The Claude layer ships only in public, synthetic-data repos. The
  proprietary 1099 / DataVault repo is never opened in Claude Code (C42 §7); it carries the
  deny-all *tripwire* `.claude/settings.json` + stop-only `CLAUDE.md` instead.
- **Size.** `CLAUDE.md` + `AGENTS.md` ≤ ~200 lines combined; push depth into skills and ADRs.

