## 🔧 Tooling Configuration

> **2026 stack:** `uv` (env + deps) · `ruff` (lint + format + import sort) · `mypy` (types).
> This collapses pip/venv, Black, isort, and flake8 into two Rust binaries — one config file.
>
> **Python version is `3.14` everywhere** (CORRECTION 28) — `requires-python`, ruff target,
> mypy target, the Docker base image and CI must agree. A mismatch means CI checks syntax
> the runtime will never see. **Standard GIL build only — never `python3.14t`.**

### Ruff (Linting + Formatting — replaces Black, isort, flake8)
```toml
# pyproject.toml
[tool.ruff]
target-version = "py314"
line-length = 88

[tool.ruff.lint]
select = [
    "E",    # pycodestyle errors
    "F",    # pyflakes
    "I",    # isort (import sorting)
    "W",    # pycodestyle warnings
    "UP",   # pyupgrade (modern Python syntax)
    "B",    # flake8-bugbear
    "SIM",  # flake8-simplify
]
ignore = ["E501"]  # line length handled by formatter

[tool.ruff.lint.isort]
known-first-party = ["src"]

[tool.ruff.format]
quote-style = "double"
```

### Formatting (`ruff format` — Black is retired)
`ruff format` is a drop-in Black replacement (~99.9% identical output, far faster) and
ships the "2026 style" in Ruff ≥ 0.15. **Do not run Black separately** — one tool, one config.
Import sorting is Ruff's `I` lint rule; no standalone `isort`.

### mypy (Type Checking)
```toml
[tool.mypy]
python_version = "3.14"
strict = false          # tighten to true as a project matures
warn_return_any = true
warn_unused_configs = true
```
> `ty` (Astral's fast type checker) is emerging and pairs with uv/ruff; mypy remains the
> reference implementation with the widest library compatibility — stay on mypy for now.

