```

### Rules
- Dockerfile lives in project root
- `.dockerignore` keeps image small and secure (no tests, no real data, no secrets)
- Multi-stage builds for production (Stage 2+ optimization)
- `--env-file .env` for API keys at runtime — never bake secrets into images
- Docker also hosts **Structurizr Lite** for local C4 rendering (see `architecture-docs.mdc`)
- The image carries **none** of the agent harness — it is development tooling, not runtime

### .gitignore — agent-harness entries
```
# Claude Code — personal, never committed. `**/` covers nested .claude/ dirs;
# a bare `.claude/...` pattern is anchored to the root and misses subdirectories.
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/CLAUDE.local.md
**/.claude/agent-memory-local/
```

