## 🚀 CI Pipeline (GitHub Actions)

Every project ships CI. The lint / type / test / eval sequence is **merge-blocking** via
a branch protection rule on `main`.

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

permissions:
  contents: read                     # least privilege — CI only reads the repo

concurrency:
  group: ci-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true           # a new push cancels the superseded run

# Every action is pinned to a full commit SHA, release in the trailing comment.
jobs:
  quality:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 20
    steps:
      - name: Check out code
        uses: actions/checkout@d23441a48e516b6c34aea4fa41551a30e30af803  # v6.1.0

      - name: Install uv and Python
        uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@bec219d24cd3e171d82865faccec33120bb574f4  # v10.1.0
        with:
          python-version: "3.14"       # CORRECTION 28 — matches requires-python
          enable-cache: true           # caches uv's package cache, keyed on uv.lock

      - name: Install locked dependencies
        run: uv sync --locked          # fails if uv.lock is stale instead of rewriting it

      - name: Cache pre-commit environments
        uses: actions/cache@0057852bfaa89a56745cba8c7296529d2fc39830  # v4.3.0
        with:
          path: ~/.cache/pre-commit
          key: pre-commit-${{ runner.os }}-${{ hashFiles('.pre-commit-config.yaml') }}

      - name: Pre-commit hooks (gitleaks · ruff · lock + hook drift · harness drift)
        run: uvx pre-commit run --all-files --show-diff-on-failure
        # Superset of the local gate: anything a --no-verify commit slipped past lands
        # here — including hook-versions-check and claude-agents/rules-check drift.

      - name: Lint
        run: uv run ruff check src/ tests/

      - name: Format check
        run: uv run ruff format --check src/ tests/

      - name: Type check
        run: uv run mypy src/

      - name: Test
        run: uv run pytest tests/ -v --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing

      - name: AI evaluation (blocking gate)
        run: uv run deepeval test run tests/test_eval.py
        env:
          DEEPEVAL_MODEL: ${{ vars.DEEPEVAL_JUDGE }}
          ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}
```

- **No `pip install ".[dev]"`** — that path predates the uv standard and bypasses the lock.
- **`--locked`, never `--frozen`, in CI.** `--frozen` would install a stale lock without
  complaint; `--locked` is what makes CI the staleness gate (the `uv-lock` hook is the
  local one). Workspaces: `uv sync --all-packages --all-groups --locked`.
- **Pin every action to a full commit SHA** with its release in a comment
  (`@d23441a…  # v6.1.0`). Tags are movable pointers; SHAs are not. `astral-sh/setup-uv`
  publishes **no floating major tag** — `@v10` fails with *Unable to resolve action* — so
  it can only be pinned by release or SHA. Resolve a release's commit SHA with
  `git ls-remote https://github.com/<owner>/<repo> 'refs/tags/<tag>*'` — when a `^{}`
  line appears (annotated tag), that line's SHA is the commit. Move pins on the
  dependency-update cadence, never by drift.
- **Python comes from `setup-uv`'s `python-version` input** — no `actions/setup-python`,
  no separate `uv python install` step.
- Cache uv, not pip.
- Harness drift (`make claude-check`) runs through the pre-commit step — no separate job.
- The eval job is a gate, not a report. See `testing-and-eval.mdc`.
